# The ACR build context is the repository root, because the instance image has
# to assemble the engine from src/. Everything that is not needed for that or
# for the Go builds is excluded — a 1 GiB sparse .dat uploaded by accident would
# turn a 20-second build into a very long one.
#
# site/assets is NOT excluded: the control-plane image serves the site, so its
# logo and hero images have to be inside it. Excluding them once cost a live
# site with no images and 404s on every asset — 1.7 MB is not worth that.

.git
.github
.hallmark
build/
poc/
examples/
tests/
clients/

# Every node_modules, not just the one that existed when this file was written.
# workload/ arrived later and brought 420 MB across three of them, which turned
# `az acr build` into a pack step that never finished uploading. Neither
# root-context image copies anything from workload/, so exclude it wholesale;
# the CDC gateway builds from its own directory as its own context and is
# unaffected by this file.
**/node_modules
workload/

docs/assets
*.dat
*.wal
*.cdc
*.bak
*.part
*.exe
*.pdb
*.log

# Local credentials. Neither image copies these, so nothing has ever reached a
# published layer — but the build context itself is uploaded to ACR and retained,
# and .gitignore already anticipates a .env holding an Entra client secret at
# exactly this path. Excluding them here means creating that file cannot quietly
# ship it to the registry on the next deploy.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy.env
